    "title": "10x Genomics Xenium Breast Cancer SpatialData with Chromium scRNA-seq Reference (CSAMA 2026)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20180722",
    "publication_date": "2026-05-14",
    "description": "<ul>\n<li>BC_10x_xenium_sdata.zarr.zip<br>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>SpatialData object containing a cropped, low-resolution representation of the 10x Genomics Xenium Prime FFPE Human Breast Cancer dataset. The object includes Xenium transcript coordinates, cell and nucleus segmentation boundaries, cell-level expression table, H&amp;E image, and four immunofluorescence channels including DAPI. High-resolution image pyramids were removed to reduce file size.</p>\n<p>Original dataset:<br><a href=\"https://www.10xgenomics.com/datasets/xenium-prime-ffpe-human-breast-cancer\">https://www.10xgenomics.com/datasets/xenium-prime-ffpe-human-breast-cancer</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>BC_scRNAseq_subset.h5ad.zip\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>AnnData object containing reference breast cancer scRNA-seq data derived from the Janesick et al. Chromium dataset. Data processing followed the OSTA workflows.</p>\n<p>Raw count matrix:<br><a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/download/?acc=GSM7782698&amp;format=file&amp;file=GSM7782698%5Fcount%5Fraw%5Ffeature%5Fbc%5Fmatrix%2Eh5\">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/download/?acc=GSM7782698&amp;format=file&amp;file=GSM7782698%5Fcount%5Fraw%5Ffeature%5Fbc%5Fmatrix%2Eh5</a></p>\n<p>Cell type annotations:<br><a href=\"https://zenodo.org/records/10076046/files/Cell_Barcode_Type_Matrices.xlsx?download=1\">https://zenodo.org/records/10076046/files/Cell_Barcode_Type_Matrices.xlsx?download=1</a></p>\n<p>Processing references:<br><a href=\"https://github.com/lmweber/STexampleData/blob/devel/inst/scripts/make-data-Janesick-breastCancer-Chromium.R\">https://github.com/lmweber/STexampleData/blob/devel/inst/scripts/make-data-Janesick-breastCancer-Chromium.R</a><br><a href=\"https://lmweber.org/OSTA/pages/seq-deconvolution.html\">https://lmweber.org/OSTA/pages/seq-deconvolution.html</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
